# Environment: torch-vibevoice
#
# PyTorch for the `vibevoice` stack alone. It is its own environment because VibeVoice caps
# transformers below 5.0.0 while FireRed pins it at exactly 5.1.0 and mlx-audio requires
# >=5.5.0 — three mutually exclusive ranges across four packages. The resolver's messages for
# all ten conflicting groupings are in
# model_tests/benchmark/results/2026-08-17-environment-partition.json.
#
# Serves the packages: vibevoice-asr-7b.
#
# **This environment is provisional.** mlx-audio 0.4.5 implements VibeVoice-ASR, and
# mlx-community publishes converted weights, so this stack can run in `mlx` with no added
# dependencies at all. It does not yet, because the MLX path is not output-equivalent: on the
# recorded CantoMap fixture it produced 47 segments where torch produced 49, shifted some
# orthography to traditional characters, and labelled one non-speech interval differently
# (model_tests/benchmark/results/2026-08-17-mlx-collapse-probes.json). Adopting it replaces
# every recorded VibeVoice figure, so it waits on re-measurement rather than on a lock change.
# When that lands, this file and its lock are deleted, not edited.
#
# The forced aligner is deliberately *not* here, though the recorded pipeline ran it in the
# same PyTorch environment. Its MLX implementation is token-identical to the recorded torch
# output across all 246 aligned tokens, so it moved to `mlx`.
#
# Citation: model_tests/vibevoice/VibeVoice/pyproject.toml [project].dependencies at checkout
# 94da20d. Server and UI extras — gradio, aiortc, uvicorn, fastapi, pydub, requests — are
# dropped: the recorded runner imports the model directly and never serves. The as-built venv
# resolved to torch 2.13.0, transformers 4.57.6, diffusers 0.39.0.
#
# The VibeVoice package itself is not listed: it is a pinned source checkout with the tracked
# `logits_to_keep` patch applied, installed with --no-deps.
#
# Python: 3.12.12, the as-built version.
# Upstream declares most of these unpinned. Left that way, the resolver picks whatever is
# newest today — numpy 2.5.2 and librosa 1.0.0 rather than the 2.4.6 and 0.11.0 that ran —
# and the lock stops describing the environment the figures came from. So each is pinned to
# its as-built version, read from dist-info under
# model_tests/vibevoice/VibeVoice/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages. Upstream's own ranges
# are kept alongside where they are narrower than the pin is.
transformers==4.57.6        # upstream range: >=4.51.3,<5.0.0
torch==2.13.0
accelerate==1.14.0
diffusers==0.39.0
librosa==0.11.0
numpy==2.4.6
scipy==1.18.0
soundfile==0.14.0
llvmlite>=0.40.0
numba>=0.57.0
